{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502271-what-would-you-change-about-blood-magic-in-vtm","id":1502271,"title":"What would you change about Blood Magic in VTM?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-02-05T19:26:18-08:00","id":1502271,"title":"What would you change about Blood Magic in VTM?","content":"I would make it to where practitioners of Blood Magic would <u><b>have</b></u> to be on a Path of Enlightenment that correlates with the Blood Magic they practice. For example, an Anarch thaumaturge that practices New Age sorcery will be on a Path of Enlightenment that correlates with New Age sorcery. I feel that it would really hit home the fact that the ability to practice Blood Magic alters the practitioner on both a mental and spiritual level.<br /> <br /> What about you?<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":27313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","user":"Hello","date":". 02-06-2023, 08:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T19:50:47-08:00","id":1502275,"title":"","content":"I would grab the VtR rules and adapt them; specifically there is a VtR supplement at the end of 1e that's actually the basis for 2e VtR blood magic too.<br /> <br /> What this does:<br /> <br /> 1) Ritual only magic. There's no need for blood magic Paths, or learning lots and lots of different sub-Disciplines. Combat blood magic is either pre-prepared rituals or rituals you can do in a few seconds. This cuts down a lot on the &quot;power gamer&quot; aspects of blood magic. Mind control blood magic will never be as good as Dominate, because you have to finish a ritual before anything happens, not because it's artificially worse in effect.<br /> <br /> 2) Functional rules for designing rituals. This can be purely OOC to help homebrew them, IC rules for magically researcher type, or even allow some level of mage-like improvised magic to come up with rituals on the fly.<br /> <br /> 3) Standardized rules for how different blood magic works. The differences are more who you can learn it from, and what costs you pay to make your magic work (which is also more fun).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-06T04:18:27-08:00","id":1502295,"title":"","content":"-Thaumaturgy and mortal hedge magic are the same thing, because thaumaturgy is something that comes from belief/willpower and thus comes from the human side of the vampire, which is why the Beast can't use it in frenzy. Mortals don't have something as convenient as Vitae, but they can get around that by sacrificing other things/ using objects charged with magic/faith.<br /> <br /> -Thaumaturges need a knowledge related to their craft. In-clan thaumaturgy needs 1 dot, caitiff, ghouls and mortals need at least 2, OoC practitioners need 3.<br /> <br /> -&quot;Dark Thaumaturgy&quot; is the art of channelling a spirit to do magic you can't do yourself. A level of Dark thaumaturgy adds to normal thaumaturgy rating. for example if you have 4 Thaumaturgy and 2 DT= you have a thaumaturgy level of 6. This works to the ninth level. DT is always learnt at in-clan costs. Using DT always comes with temporary side effects but in-of-itself can't do permanent damage to a vampiric user. Dealing with spirits and &quot;demons&quot; itself can be difficult, and usually means additional burdens on the user. Even in cases where the contract is favourable or the spirit is tightly controlled by the user, which is a difficult thing to achieve, DT is highly stigmatized as Vampires hate those who can quickly gain powers and upset the social order.<br /> <br /> -There's a lot of extremely minor/novel powers that practitioners can learn without xp. These have very little mechanical power but serve to make the world more interesting. If it exists, there's magic for it.<br /> <br /> <br /> -Rituals are learnt during downtime. Using downtime for rituals means you're not gaining other backgrounds which could also be gained during downtime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 02-06-2023, 07:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-06T15:56:56-08:00","id":1502329,"title":"","content":"The change for blood magic that needs to happen is the XP sink nature of the systems. Every White Wolf game line seems to have one mechanic section that requires an absurd amount of XP to level up. For VtM it is all the magic paths, in exalted it was martial arts and crafting, in werewolf it was so many charms, etc.<br /> <br /> You can make a fully functional combat character build for around 75 xp post character creation and have plenty of options. Playing a &quot;mage&quot; means you can easily burn through 250+ xp post character creation and still not be all that well rounded as a caster character. In short, the gaming group is more likely to break up or start a different game before you get to actually play your character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-06T18:30:09-08:00","id":1502335,"title":"","content":"I'd remove all Paths and let it only be a matter of rituals. This is a drum I've been part of beating on for a long time and which I will continue to beat on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-06T21:11:52-08:00","id":1502340,"title":"","content":"Rituals-only here too, but the Tremere have the explicitly unique advantage of being able to hammer five Rituals of roughly escalating scale into a <b>Form</b>, which can be learned like a Discipline. Which is important for the Warlocks, since in my head-WoD the Tremere are actually all Caitiff and are only a Clan in the socio-political sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T01:05:41-08:00","id":1502357,"title":"","content":"I think ritual-only is kinda... ok, it's not crazy, but I don't see the point. <br /> 1- Why get rid of paths when they're balanced by XP and are extremely niche? <br /> 2: if you're just doing rituals what's the point in making it a discipline? Sabbat rituals don't need a discipline. <br /> <br /> Thematically I don't like it because I like the whole willworking stuff, but I recognize that's very subjective. I think on a societal scale Path Magic is great because it projects a level of power and awe that causes Thaumaturgy to be coveted, feared and jealously horded in a way you wouldn't get if you just had path magic. Mechanically? There's nothing wrong with paths and you're just taking out a fun thing for no reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T01:43:28-08:00","id":1502365,"title":"","content":"I think it worth noting that I rise up Protean as an important and thematic antithesis to Thaumaturgy. Thaumaturgy comes from the soul, Protean is the Beast manifest and comes in a thousand forms. Level 1 Protean isn't just Eyes of the Beast, it could also be Ears of the Bat, Nose of the wolf, Pits of the viper, Ampullae of the shark, Chameleon skin, Serpents gaze... This also costs a lot of XP, and there are a few ritual elements in there too. Just as a vampire can devote themselves to magic or social connections, vampires can also push themselves towards becoming perfect predators. Other methods like Vicissitude, necromancy or Abyss mysticism are also time and XP consuming ways for vampires to elevate themselves (but are considered extremely heterodox by most vampires) <br /> <br /> within this context it makes a lot of sense for Thaumaturgy to be something you can really delve into, but I can see why you'd want to go the opposite route and cut down the options so that vampires are more materially invested creatures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T03:06:15-08:00","id":1502370,"title":"","content":"What would I be cutting in an all ritual system based on late VtR 1e/VtR 2e's methods? Again, those come with a more much exhaustive guide to making your own rituals. As I noted on three different levels of appeal to play, you can design any ritual you want. You can adjust the thematic tone of the rituals to help ensure they fit your group's vision of what vampire blood magic should look like. You also don't have to worry about what should be a Path and what should be a ritual. Why did studying if a vampire can control fire turn into Lure of the Flames instead of a few rituals that allow various levels of pyromancy? Why does Levin Bolt just get better and better lightning bolts to shoot at people, while Path of Blood has five distinct powers?<br /> <br /> Going all ritual makes it all easier to do because it all follows a more coherent set of design principles. It's more accessible as a rule, which tends to be more fun. Since you can remake any power as a ritual on some level, no power or ability is actually being cut from the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T06:23:52-08:00","id":1502385,"title":"","content":"I'd bring back weather-control. It's a classic Dracula power, and very visually cool. I hate that it has been retconned into nonexistence and that Thaum is just all blood tricks now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T07:19:27-08:00","id":1502389,"title":"","content":"I tend to have a hard and fast rule that blood magic cannot. Predict the future, heal or do necromancy. V5 blood sorcery is pretty silly and is one of the reasons i abandoned the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T10:55:54-08:00","id":1502399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502271-what-would-you-change-about-blood-magic-in-vtm?p=1502389#post1502389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tend to have a hard and fast rule that blood magic cannot Predict the future</div> </div> </div> </div>To a limited extent, yeah, all-encompassing fate sucks, but using stars or spirits and the like to make well informed predictions (weather, stocks, the sex of a baby) is like, half of what magic was used for in ancient times.<br /> <br /> Also I like a Macbeth style self fulfilling prophecy. Do I think you should be able to do that kind of thing with Thaumaturgy? No. But I'd love to play a Malkavian with a lot of tricks trying to convince people of it. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T11:02:37-08:00","id":1502401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502271-what-would-you-change-about-blood-magic-in-vtm#post1502271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would make it to where practitioners of Blood Magic would <u><b>have</b></u> to be on a Path of Enlightenment that correlates with the Blood Magic they practice. For example, an Anarch thaumaturge that practices New Age sorcery will be on a Path of Enlightenment that correlates with New Age sorcery. I feel that it would really hit home the fact that the ability to practice Blood Magic alters the practitioner on both a mental and spiritual level.<br /> <br /> What about you?<br /> <br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting takes and I don't see an issue with it. But I don't play blood mages in general and never had a strong desire to play one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T11:23:15-08:00","id":1502402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502271-what-would-you-change-about-blood-magic-in-vtm?p=1502399#post1502399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To a limited extent, yeah, all-encompassing fate sucks, but using stars or spirits and the like to make well informed predictions (weather, stocks, the sex of a baby) is like, half of what magic was used for in ancient times.<br /> <br /> Also I like a Macbeth style self fulfilling prophecy. Do I think you should be able to do that kind of thing with Thaumaturgy? No. But I'd love to play a Malkavian with a lot of tricks trying to convince people of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its partly due to malkavians (and the capppadicians to a lessor) why I don't tend to allow scrying via thaumaturgy. I also like some limits on what you can do vs true magic.<br /> <br /> I also tend to frown upon not toxic dynamics with spirits","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T12:30:35-08:00","id":1502413,"title":"","content":"Surely the many Paths became quite the mess and many times only NPCs can really shine with them, like having 20+ dots among different paths etc. I would like the idea to make it Rituals, but then we would need different ritual branches to give more flavour and a sense of development in the skill of the blood mage. For instance, a school of rituals related to weather control, blood magic, pyromancy, etc. Also, there should be a way for blood magic to compete with physical attacks in terms of damage, in my decades of experience as a ST players often complain that it's basically impossible for a Thaumaturge to compete with a vampire with celerity and potence, this could be somehow accomplished by creating powerful rituals that uses good dicepools or a system similar to the way Arete influence damage of Magicks, using a table, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12348,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","user":"Herr Meister","date":". 02-07-2023, 04:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-04T11:38:55-08:00","id":1504375,"title":"","content":"The only thing I can think of would be to make Blood Magic more viable by reducing the cost, like you only spend 5xp on each level except the last one, but your abilities are only useful in certain situations or as if used with prior preparation like &quot;Corrosive Vitae&quot;, &quot;Taste of Blood&quot;, &quot;Scorpion's Touch&quot;, &quot;Mirror Forge&quot;, to name a few. For the paths, it would work like this, you would have a main path and a secondary path, the primary path would cost 3xp plus level -1, the secondary 3xp plus level and the other paths would cost the normal 5xp plus level, maybe that could unbalance the game, but is what I can think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-04T22:03:54-08:00","id":1504411,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of people without Thaumaturgy being able to perform Rituals. They'd need to pay XP for it per Ritual, as opposed to those with proper dots in Blood Sorcery who can learn Rituals with time alone.<br /> <br /> As I recall, DAV20 did something like this, albeit to a limited degree.<br /> <br /> It just seems like there's a lot of powers common to vampire lore that are locked up into Blood Sorcery, when they should be more common. Like the ability to crawl along walls, a classic Dracula staple.<br /> <br /> Moreover, it kind of makes sense that, especially prior to the rise of the Tremere and their effective monopoly on Blood Sorcery within the Camarilla, there was likely a brisk trade in magical secrets among vampires throughout history. Tricks that Sires then passed on to Childer, as needed. So there's always the possibility that a vampire the PCs encounter might have a one-off magic power they didn't expect. Making research into their enemies all the more important, to spot and circumvent such tricks.<br /> <br /> Long time users on the forum might also remember years ago, when I came up with the concept of Malkavians learning Blood Sorcery through the Malkavian Madness Network. Because if you have what is effectively a low grade hive mind connecting a whole Clan, some of whom have been around for thousands of years, you're going to get magical concepts bleeding into the brains of random Lunatics. Either accidentally or intentionally. Dots in Mentor might represent an older Malk, versed in magic, knowingly or unknowingly feeding lore to the PC despite them never having been in the same room before.<br /> <br /> Assuming the &quot;Mentor&quot; is even still unalive, rather than a mass of arcane knowledge being shuffled around the cobweb for lack of any permanent residence. The PC grasping hold of whatever scraps of lore they can from their seizure-inducing arcana hallucinations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-05T06:46:39-08:00","id":1504420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502271-what-would-you-change-about-blood-magic-in-vtm?p=1504411#post1504411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea of people without Thaumaturgy being able to perform Rituals. They'd need to pay XP for it per Ritual, as opposed to those with proper dots in Blood Sorcery who can learn Rituals with time alone.<br /> <br /> As I recall, DAV20 did something like this, albeit to a limited degree.<br /> <br /> It just seems like there's a lot of powers common to vampire lore that are locked up into Blood Sorcery, when they should be more common. Like the ability to crawl along walls, a classic Dracula staple.<br /> <br /> Moreover, it kind of makes sense that, especially prior to the rise of the Tremere and their effective monopoly on Blood Sorcery within the Camarilla, there was likely a brisk trade in magical secrets among vampires throughout history. Tricks that Sires then passed on to Childer, as needed. So there's always the possibility that a vampire the PCs encounter might have a one-off magic power they didn't expect. Making research into their enemies all the more important, to spot and circumvent such tricks.<br /> <br /> Long time users on the forum might also remember years ago, when I came up with the concept of Malkavians learning Blood Sorcery through the Malkavian Madness Network. Because if you have what is effectively a low grade hive mind connecting a whole Clan, some of whom have been around for thousands of years, you're going to get magical concepts bleeding into the brains of random Lunatics. Either accidentally or intentionally. Dots in Mentor might represent an older Malk, versed in magic, knowingly or unknowingly feeding lore to the PC despite them never having been in the same room before.<br /> <br /> Assuming the &quot;Mentor&quot; is even still unalive, rather than a mass of arcane knowledge being shuffled around the cobweb for lack of any permanent residence. The PC grasping hold of whatever scraps of lore they can from their seizure-inducing arcana hallucinations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Look, you can get to the wall like a spider or something, I think it can be done if you are strong enough to cling to, when you arrest I think it is possible with the protean, vicissitude and spiritus disciplines. About Malkavian Learning tricks and rituals through the madness network, I think it would be very unbalanced to use in a chronicle, except in very special cases or in NPCs, I mean, which would prevent him from learning secrets or gaining aptitude in all existing disciplines?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-05T09:49:14-08:00","id":1504443,"title":"","content":"Presumably, you should be able to climb many ordinarily impossible things with a few levels of Potence. If you can get your finger tips into, say, masonry, and you possess supernatural strength without any weight gain, it should be quite easy to climb. Pro-climbers IRL can do some crazy shit you wouldn't think they could do without seeing it, imagining them with unreasonable strength and stamina would really be quite an alarming sight. It isn't quite Spider-man's magical sticking ability, but I think you need to understand how <i>absurdly broken</i> it would be to have that an easily acquired power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-05T20:40:14-08:00","id":1504531,"title":"","content":"I played a mortal hedge-magician that used Blood-magic, non-ghoul. The besting obstacle was getting vitae from vamps. <br /> <br /> And I don't suggest Weather-control; that was one of the most powerful powers a Mummy could have. I could bring down nations with it and only be a starting-character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T05:51:32-08:00","id":1504582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502271-what-would-you-change-about-blood-magic-in-vtm?p=1504531#post1504531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I played a mortal hedge-magician that used Blood-magic, non-ghoul. The besting obstacle was getting vitae from vamps.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did any Kindred attempt to make her or him into a Ghoul during this playthrough? And if I may ask, how did this spellcaster character came to spellcasting inclinations and methods derived from blood, pleasure, sadism, or predation? Did she or he for example read through books and tomes or practice meditation to get a decent enough start in learning?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-07T01:13:55-08:00","id":1504735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502271-what-would-you-change-about-blood-magic-in-vtm?p=1502357#post1502357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1- Why get rid of paths when they're balanced by XP and are extremely niche?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think they really are, at least the old (pre V5) rules basically to go for secondary paths with a strong power at level 1 or 2 (or maybe 3) grab those and move to the next path.<br /> <br /> Path were you get the good stuff only at higher levels, or that had only one power that got better with increasing level (like Lure of Flames or Movement of mind) got expensive pretty fast.<br /> <br /> But to be fair regular disciplines have in some cases the same problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-07T04:49:49-08:00","id":1504747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aahz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502271-what-would-you-change-about-blood-magic-in-vtm?p=1504735#post1504735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think they really are, at least the old (pre V5) rules basically to go for secondary paths with a strong power at level 1 or 2 (or maybe 3) grab those and move to the next path.<br /> <br /> Path were you get the good stuff only at higher levels, or that had only one power that got better with increasing level (like Lure of Flames or Movement of mind) got expensive pretty fast.<br /> <br /> But to be fair regular disciplines have in some cases the same problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's like... the same for skills, knowledges and Disciplines, which I'd argue are MORE bottom heavy most of the time. +2 difficulty, or not being able to roll gives you a lot of encouragement to go wide rather than deep with these abilities, and as for Disciplines, like, as powerful as 4's and 5's can be the ones you actually want most are in the 1-3 range. Never mind diminishing returns, the level 1 power for most disciplines (All Disciplines if we discount the more poorly written disciplines) are broadly applicable tools, while 4's and 5's are extremely specialized powers that are reserved for specific contexts. Many of the most prolific thaumaturgy paths are the opposite, only really being worthwhile once you get to the third level, with a few outliers that are better for dipping. <br /> <br /> <br /> Mind you, the first level of a Path is relatively expensive. 7xp, 4xp for the second level, then 8,12, 16... Like going wide with Thaumaturgy isn't immediately better than going deep or investing somewhere else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-07T06:56:46-08:00","id":1504750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502271-what-would-you-change-about-blood-magic-in-vtm?p=1504747#post1504747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Many of the most prolific thaumaturgy paths are the opposite, only really being worthwhile once you get to the third level, with a few outliers that are better for dipping.</div> </div> </div> </div>Path of Mars and Neptune's Might are really interesting, cool, and nice as obscure, rare, and characterful Paths that still prove to be very useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-07T09:27:09-08:00","id":1504764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502271-what-would-you-change-about-blood-magic-in-vtm?p=1504750#post1504750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Path of Mars and Neptune's Might are really interesting, cool, and nice as obscure, rare, and characterful Paths that still prove to be very useful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Path of Mars is garbage.<br /> Neptune's might is... strong, In v20 I don't see a limit to <i>dehydrate</i>. <i>Goodbye Pacific</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /> Personally though, abilities/attributes weigh more when it comes to making your character better/strong. Disciplines are <i>flashy </i>and <i>exotic </i>and get people excited, and paths moreso, but mundane ability is the most important thing your character needs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 03-07-2023, 01:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-07T09:52:33-08:00","id":1504766,"title":"","content":"I quite like path of Mars because im all about thematics over raw power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-07T09:54:45-08:00","id":1504767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502271-what-would-you-change-about-blood-magic-in-vtm?p=1504764#post1504764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neptune's might is... strong, In v20 I don't see a limit to <i>dehydrate</i>. <i>Goodbye Pacific</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;At this level of mastery, the thaumaturge can directly<br /> attack living and unliving targets by removing the<br /> water from their bodies. Victims killed by this power<br /> leave behind hideous mummified corpses. This power<br /> can also be used for less aggressive purposes, such as<br /> drying out wet clothes \u2014 or evaporating puddles to<br /> keep other practitioners of this path from using them.\u200b&quot;<br /> <br /> Seems to indicate living creature or smaller sizes, unless you are making an argument about the Pacific Ocean being classified as a puddle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-07T18:06:20-08:00","id":1504796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502271-what-would-you-change-about-blood-magic-in-vtm?p=1504582#post1504582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did any Kindred attempt to make her or him into a Ghoul during this playthrough? And if I may ask, how did this spellcaster character came to spellcasting inclinations and methods derived from blood, pleasure, sadism, or predation? Did she or he for example read through books and tomes or practice meditation to get a decent enough start in learning?</div> </div> </div> </div>Through tomes, alchemy and practice; first, I first created the character in <i>Mage: the Ascension</i>, and then converted it to <i>Masquerade</i>. Vampire-blood was tass, so, it worked. But, I created that character before I read <i>Second Sight</i>, which cleared up hedge-magicians greatly. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-14T15:40:08-07:00","id":1505380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502271-what-would-you-change-about-blood-magic-in-vtm?p=1502365#post1502365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it worth noting that I rise up Protean as an important and thematic antithesis to Thaumaturgy. Thaumaturgy comes from the soul, Protean is the Beast manifest and comes in a thousand forms. Level 1 Protean isn't just Eyes of the Beast, it could also be Ears of the Bat, Nose of the wolf, Pits of the viper, Ampullae of the shark, Chameleon skin, Serpents gaze... This also costs a lot of XP, and there are a few ritual elements in there too. Just as a vampire can devote themselves to magic or social connections, vampires can also push themselves towards becoming perfect predators. Other methods like Vicissitude, necromancy or Abyss mysticism are also time and XP consuming ways for vampires to elevate themselves (but are considered extremely heterodox by most vampires)<br /> <br /> within this context it makes a lot of sense for Thaumaturgy to be something you can really delve into, but I can see why you'd want to go the opposite route and cut down the options so that vampires are more materially invested creatures.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't it also semi-canon(depending on book) that Serpentis and Viscisitude are offshoots of Protean? It'd kind of make sense that the discipline about becoming a mutable creature has a large number of variants and abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-14T16:49:59-07:00","id":1505388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502271-what-would-you-change-about-blood-magic-in-vtm?p=1505380#post1505380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Isn't it also semi-canon(depending on book) that Serpentis and Viscisitude are offshoots of Protean? It'd kind of make sense that the discipline about becoming a mutable creature has a large number of variants and abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>In V5 this applies for granted and in the case of serpentis, it even makes sense if you think that the discipline was corrupted by Set which creates the association with snakes and also considering that the clan has a variant with protean. In the case of Vicissitude I feel a little inclined to disagree, in my view the protean imitates something that already exists, such as animals, mixing with earth or even mist, homever vicissitude makes you capable of molding the flesh into something different so instead of imitating you in theory create something new.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-14T17:44:29-07:00","id":1505394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502271-what-would-you-change-about-blood-magic-in-vtm?p=1505388#post1505388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In V5 this applies for granted and in the case of serpentis, it even makes sense if you think that the discipline was corrupted by Set which creates the association with snakes and also considering that the clan has a variant with protean. In the case of Vicissitude I feel a little inclined to disagree, in my view the protean imitates something that already exists, such as animals, mixing with earth or even mist, homever vicissitude makes you capable of molding the flesh into something different so instead of imitating you in theory create something new.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's last part isn't necessarily true. For example: Elder Protean has several odd power that can allow you to do things like crawl in torpor, which doesn't imitate anything so much as master your (im)mortal form.<br /> <br /> Personally see it more as all are &quot;Form Mastery&quot; powers focused on perfecting one's form. Protean is focused on perfection in the natural world, Serpentis focused on the perfection of set/the gods, and Vicissitude is focused on perfection of life/evolution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-14T18:16:13-07:00","id":1505398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502271-what-would-you-change-about-blood-magic-in-vtm?p=1505394#post1505394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's last part isn't necessarily true. For example: Elder Protean has several odd power that can allow you to do things like crawl in torpor, which doesn't imitate anything so much as master your (im)mortal form.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you sure? I think there are some animals that do this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-14T18:55:41-07:00","id":1505402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502271-what-would-you-change-about-blood-magic-in-vtm?p=1505398#post1505398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are you sure? I think there are some animals that do this.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not believe normal animals also have the ability to return shapeshifters to their natural forms, Shape-shift to immediately resist the last source of damage they just took, or fire impaled objects at projectile capacity. The power Inward Focus(temporarily optimize your body to get a bunch of extra actions, damage, and soak) is straight up something I'd expect to see in Vicissitude rather than protean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-14T21:43:22-07:00","id":1505412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502271-what-would-you-change-about-blood-magic-in-vtm?p=1505402#post1505402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I do not believe normal animals also have the ability to return shapeshifters to their natural forms, Shape-shift to immediately resist the last source of damage they just took, or fire impaled objects at projectile capacity. The power Inward Focus(temporarily optimize your body to get a bunch of extra actions, damage, and soak) is straight up something I'd expect to see in Vicissitude rather than protean.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean walks or crawls while hibernating, it was an arthropod type I think, now this ability forces a shapershifter to revert back to normal I think it just reverses/stops the process.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-15T02:09:05-07:00","id":1505419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502271-what-would-you-change-about-blood-magic-in-vtm?p=1505412#post1505412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean walks or crawls while hibernating, it was an arthropod type I think, now this ability forces a shapershifter to revert back to normal I think it just reverses/stops the process.</div> </div> </div> </div>My point was that Protean does not only &quot;imitate what already exists&quot;, it 100% has powers that allow the user to make something new with sufficient mastery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-17T15:03:07-07:00","id":1505595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502271-what-would-you-change-about-blood-magic-in-vtm?p=1505380#post1505380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Isn't it also semi-canon(depending on book) that Serpentis and Viscisitude are offshoots of Protean? It'd kind of make sense that the discipline about becoming a mutable creature has a large number of variants and abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Serpentis has always been teased as a Protean knock off both by in-character and out of character writings. Only v5 has gone ahead and merged them. The gangrel say it's an offshoot and the setites are in deep denial for religious reasons. <br /> <br /> Vicissitude has never been seriously considered as a protean variation until V5. It has some superficial similarities but literally everyone with some measure of learning and knowledge, in character and out, has always posited Vicis as something alien and distinctly different from Protean. The Gangrel don't think it's related and the Tzmisce don't think it's related.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-18T14:56:14-07:00","id":1505708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502271-what-would-you-change-about-blood-magic-in-vtm?p=1505595#post1505595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Serpentis has always been teased as a Protean knock off both by in-character and out of character writings. Only v5 has gone ahead and merged them. The gangrel say it's an offshoot and the setites are in deep denial for religious reasons.<br /> <br /> Vicissitude has never been seriously considered as a protean variation until V5. It has some superficial similarities but literally everyone with some measure of learning and knowledge, in character and out, has always posited Vicis as something alien and distinctly different from Protean. The Gangrel don't think it's related and the Tzmisce don't think it's related.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gonna be honest, I've had a knee-jerk reaction to ignore the lore relating to &quot;alien origins of Vicissitude&quot; after what happened with the original black hand supplement. I've been avoiding anything that even Hints at the botched &quot;Souleater&quot; lore like the plague.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-19T01:07:53-07:00","id":1505765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502271-what-would-you-change-about-blood-magic-in-vtm?p=1505708#post1505708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Gonna be honest, I've had a knee-jerk reaction to ignore the lore relating to &quot;alien origins of Vicissitude&quot; after what happened with the original black hand supplement. I've been avoiding anything that even Hints at the botched &quot;Souleater&quot; lore like the plague.</div> </div> </div> </div> Me neither but vissitude always felt mechanically and thematically differant enough to be distinct from protean in terms of how it worked and was used. It's like the dynamic between presence, animalism and Dominate .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-19T08:01:20-07:00","id":1505784,"title":"","content":"Vicissitude Space ghost aliens is silly bs (though I do put a lot of in-character prejudice against vicissitude users and it is a belief some could conceivably hold) but disregarding that there's a lot to keep it apart<br /> <br /> Protean is temporary, vis is permanent Protean is tied to the Beast and a rejection of human tools. Vis is all about the physical form and the application of human knowledge. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-20T05:07:07-07:00","id":1505893,"title":"","content":"Yeah, &quot;alien&quot; doesn't have to be literal. Vicissitude is alien in the sense that it is beyond humanity, or antithetical to it, or at least, to your understanding of humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-21T11:46:21-07:00","id":1506054,"title":"","content":"As I imagine it, the common 7 disciplines are very human, they're human+ abilities. Now, as I run with the idea of &quot;how you hunt determines your discipline spread&quot; (and what you hunt adds to your attributes) it can be said that those who develop Potence are generally less pleasant than those who develop Obfuscate. Rarer disciplines need more than that<br /> <br /> Protean needs intuition and a kind of inward looking or Beast communion. <br /> Serpentis is just Protean but through a lense of faith. <br /> Chimestry requires you to be able to lie to yourself. <br /> Thaumaturgy needs knowledge and self enhancement rituals. these in turn need resources and security. <br /> Necromancy needs a lot of involvement (and occasional defiling) of death, corpses and ghosts and is thus for weirdos. <br /> Vicissitude needs a lot of practice to get right, and there's no undo button, so you're going to kill a lot of puppies before you can reliably craft hellhounds, ruin a lot of faces before you can create beauty, and you're going to need a really big hole to hide all the bodies.<br /> Using Obtenebration is like asking for hell's help in making you the best at mass murder. Abyss mystics are worse than your average low-key infernalist. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}